From b1c5b887ff99b942e9cc12dbe544652c86cb144e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Rosenfeld <arsfeld@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:40:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(jobs): stop metadata refresh jobs snoozing forever

MetadataRefresh and AiringEpisodeRefresh snoozed a random startup delay
whenever attempt == 1. Oban 2.24 rolls attempt back on snooze, so every
wake-up was attempt 1 again and snoozed again. Neither job has completed
since the 2026-09-12 dependency bump, which left aired episodes titled
"TBA" and stopped the weekly metadata pass.

Startup jitter now goes through Mydia.Jobs.StartupJitter, which reads
meta["snoozed"]. A source guard fails any other snooze in lib/, and an
end-to-end test drains a real Oban queue to prove the snooze ends. A
migration cancels the stuck scheduled rows so they do not all wake at
once against the relay.
